{"agent_id":"pp3g-f07i-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-c05e","agent_seq":6,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T02:54:34.975677348Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"bf000f09-c4e8-4b55-b0a7-febd4578d2d2","comment_uuid":"daa5b3ca-de61-44bb-af52-0946de90665f","author":"pp3g-f07i-you-are-one-of-several-independent-adversarial-c05e","content":"# Adversarial Review — scripts/observer/observer.sh + tests/run-tests.sh @ main HEAD\n\nVERDICT: **CONDITIONAL** — core mechanics are sound and spec-mapped (harness 98/98), but several first-principles defects (silent breaker suppression with no retry, state-loss on corrupt JSON, unbounded growth, /tmp tamper surface, and mutating-path error swallowing) must be fixed before the Execution Engine wave can trust this as a mechanical supervisor.\n\n---\n\n## 1 — Completeness vs dispatch specs (lifecycle-manager-design.md SC1-SC5 + #460 consolidated spec R1-R4/F1-F6 + data-retention.md)\n\n- R1 rename: PASS — `OBSERVER_*`/`OB_*`/state dir `/tmp/opencode/observer-state` used throughout. No residual `LIFECYCLE_*`.\n- R2 deliverable check: PASS with extension — `git diff --name-only merge-base..branch` + per-file `git cat-file -e branch:path` (observer.sh:898-935). Correctly defeats empty-branch false-positive. **Gap:** checks only first 20 files (`files[:20]` line 925); branch with >20 files still passes if first 20 are empty renames, and rename-only delta where old path deleted counts as deliverable even if no new content. Minor.\n- R3 harness triage T3/T5/T8/T4: PASS — real preservation check, space-tolerant JSON, merge via real commit, interactive shell `exit <code>` probe (run-tests.sh:103-147).\n- R4 suite green: PASS — 98/98 claimed green.\n- F1 evidence-at-transition: PASS — `compose_transition_evidence` (777-800) writes 6-section bundle (`opencode-tail.log`, `pane-tail.txt`, `git-status.txt`, `git-diffstat.txt`, `verdict-timeline.json`, `hub-position.json`) with `bundle.json` sha256 manifest, called from `act_completed`/`act_finished_unmarkable`/`act_failed`/`act_killed`/`act_frozen`. Compact `evidence_summary_line` posted to working issue.\n- F2 fast path: PASS — byte-offset cursor `read_new_log_lines` (1632-1671) + `classify_log_line` (1613-1630) + dedup `fastpath_seen` + same-cycle `act_parked`/alert. Rotation/truncation/partial-line handling implemented.\n- F3 commit-age: PASS — `commit_age_min` via `git log -1 %ct` feeds `RUNNING-ALIVE` overdue dedup and `STALE-SUSPECT` accelerated/graced escalation (1245-1266, 1306-1343).\n- F4 dual-store backup: PASS with caveats — hot `.backup` of `main:opencode.db`+`fork:opencode-fork-pp3g.db`, export FROM snapshot via `file:...?immutable=1`, microsecond stamp collision fix, index keyed `(store,session_id)`, GREEN-gated watermark, `verification.log` GREEN/RED, sync-pending local mode, prune-gate REPORT ONLY. Open gaps listed below (generation cap semantics, watermark coupling, remote read-back hashing fragility).\n- F5 admission: PASS — `admission_checks` per KICKOFF.md (model vs live `opencode models {provider}` TTL cache, issue-exists/claimed, estimate regex), `events.jsonl` audit trail, no plugin files, deduped alert. `OBSERVER_MODELS_CMD` override keeps tests deterministic.\n- F6 wave-anomaly: PASS — scan-based `wave_prev_active` vs `scanned` vanishing detection with episode dedup and re-arm (2386-2419). Correctly ignores phase-degradation.\n- Data-retention policy adherence: PASS — hot/cold split, rclone sync, extraction-before-pruning, green-gated pruning (pruning operator-manual v1 per 111-117 comments). Policy says `~/opencode-archive/` compressed JSONL + uncompressed index under archive; implementation matches (`exports/<date>/` + `index/<store>.ndx`).\n\n**Missing scope (design section “Wave-level actions” p96-102):** LIFECYCLE design lists `docs/SESSION-END.md` full wind-down and `scripts/wind-down.py` via archive policy; Observer implements per-agent cleanup but does NOT invoke the session wind-down protocol — intentional per-#460 scope (wind-down deferred), not a defect, but the claim “Lifecycle Manager owns full loop” overstates what this seed implements.\n\n---\n\n## 2 — Findings (numbered, severity, file:line evidence)\n\n### CRITICAL\n\n**F-C1 — Circuit-breaker silently drops lifecycle actions with no retry; dedup then blocks forever (SC1/SC2 violation).** `post_comment`/`kickoff_cleanup`/`kickoff_stop` gate on `breaker_allow` (473-488, 495-496, 830-831, 847). When tripped, they return `False` and `act_*` still marks `handled[\"VERDICT\"]=now_iso()` (968,1019,1064,1095,1130). Next cycle the `if \"VERDICT\" not in handled` guard prevents any retry — the cleanup/kill is permanently lost though the agent remains dirty/frozen. A burst wave (N agents completing within one hour) legitimately exhausts the 24-action cap; the ones gated by the window never get cleaned. Needs either (a) do not mark handled when breaker blocked, or (b) differentiate “attempted” vs “succeeded” and re-queue.\n\n**F-C2 — `load_state` silently falls back to `{}` on JSON corruption (data loss of breaker window, dedup, watermarks, parked phase).** `load_state` (450-456) catches `(OSError, ValueError)` and returns `{}` with no event. A torn `manager-state.json` (power loss mid-`os.replace`, or tamper under `/tmp`) discards `action_window`, `fastpath_seen`, `admission_alerted`, `backup.watermarks`, `agents[].phase/stale_streak/resume_at`. Next cycle watermarks reset to `0` causing duplicate export, dedup forgotten (duplicate alerts), parked agents forgotten (premature re-park). Should log `state-load-failed` with size/hash and attempt `STATE_FILE.bak` recovery or refuse to advance.\n\n**F-C3 — Tamperable mutable state under world-readable `/tmp`.** `OBSERVER_STATE_DIR=/tmp/opencode/observer-state` (186) `mkdir -p .../evidence` (300) with default umask, `manager-state.json` (398) written atomically but unsigned/unchecked, `events.jsonl` append-only (336-434). Any local user/process can modify `manager-state.json` to reset `action_window` (defeat breaker), forge `handled` to suppress kills, or advance `watermarks` to skip archive coverage. The “everything evidence-hashed” claim in the brief is true for evidence bundles (`bundle.json` sha256 per file) but NOT for the durable decision store itself. Needs restrictive `chmod 0700` + ownership check or hash chain, and should not ceil to “surface-independent” if trust is `/tmp`.\n\n### MAJOR\n\n**F-M1 — Mutating-path `crosslink`/`git`/`sqlite3`/`tmux`/`rclone` failures swallowed; operator sees no failure except an events.jsonl line.** `post_comment` logs `posted: rc==0` (503-505) then returns False — callers in `act_failed`/`act_killed`/`act_frozen` and `wave_doctrine`/`wave_admission` ignore the False (975,1020,1085,1115,1157). `kickoff_cleanup`/`kickoff_stop` log rc/out/err (840-841,856-857) then return bool; `act_*` records `cleanup_ok` in the staging row/chain but never alerts when `False` in non-dry-run (except via `orphan` sweep flag one cycle later). If `crosslink` binary missing or `sqlite3 .backup` fails (1792-1794), the operator at the flag issue (#429) sees silence; forensic discovery sinks to `events.jsonl` archaeology — exactly the problem Observer was to eliminate. Mutating failures need an explicit `[OBSERVER][ERROR]` comment or a retry, not just a staged-field flip.\n\n**F-M2 — `set -u` without `set -e`/`pipefail`; pipeline failures in the bash loop are silently ignored.** Top-level `set -u` only (167). The per-cycle shell pipeline `printf … | python3 -c 'json.dumps …'` (2469-2471) and `printf … | python3 -c \"$CYCLE_PROG\" 2>>…` (2475) never check `PIPESTATUS`. If `python3` is missing or the JSON is truncated, `compact` may be empty and the code takes the `json-parse-failed` branch (2472) but still counts as `consecutive_errors=0` (2466) before the branch, masking the error from the consecutive-error cap. The Python side `run()` catches `FileNotFoundError`->127 but the bash side does not propagate `liveness_rc` correctly when `out` is empty but rc=0 (e.g., `python3 \"$LIVENESS_PY\" --json --all` prints nothing on error). Should add `set -o pipefail` and treat empty/parse-failed as a consecutive error.\n\n**F-M3 — State-save failure logged but loop continues with divergent in-memory vs on-disk state.** `save_state` returns `err` string (458-466); `main()` logs `state-save-failed` (2424-2426) but still prints the cycle summary as success (`rc` from `sys.exit(main())` ==0) and the bash loop does not treat it as a consecutive error (2476-2483). Next cycle `load_state` will read the stale file, re-emit deduped alerts, double-count `action_window`, etc. Schedule divergence is silent. Should treat save failure as cycle error and halt/retry per the two-principles requirement (cheapest falsifier is the save rc itself).\n\n**F-M4 — Backup watermark coupling: one RED table starves the other table’s watermark in the same store.** `store_green` flag (2020-2021, 2039-2041, 2055-2074) is per-store, but `green_wms` is per `(store,table)`. If `session` exports GREEN and `session_v2` fails verification (RED), `store_green` becomes False and **neither** table’s watermark advances, so the already-GREEN table will be re-exported every wave (duplicate artifacts, unbounded archive growth) until the sibling table heals. Spec is per-table isolation (watermark per `(store,table)`). Fix: advance per-table independently; only block pruning report for the affected table.\n\n**F-M5 — Unbounded growth: `events.jsonl`, `python-stderr.log`, `evidence/` never rotated/pruned; evidence bundles live under `/tmp` which is the same filesystem as the archive hot-backup check.** Growth counters: one `cycle` event per 120s + per-transition bundle (6 files) + backup `GREEN`/`RED` lines + `verification.log`/`sync-pending.log`/`prune-report.txt`. No cap in `observer.sh`; `data-retention.md` governs session archives, not observer-state. On a long swarm (hours) the evidence dir can exhaust the same `disk_usage(ARCHIVE_DIR).free` guard (1785) that protects hot-backups, causing backup abort (`insufficient-disk`) while evidence is the filler. Needs a retention/cap for `events.jsonl` (logrotate or size gate) and evidence expiry (e.g., keep last N bundles per agent).\n\n**F-M6 — Log-attribution brittleness to schema drift.** `agent_log_section` (511-585) depends on `message=created` + `directory=` marker then `session.id=…` and `llm.provider=/llm.model=` patterns that are OpenCode v1/v2 fork specifics. If the log format omits `directory=` (headless probe) or renames `llm.provider` to `llm.providerID`, `result[\"sessions\"]` stays empty and `result[\"available\"]` false, so `parse_retry_after` and `rate_limited` classification fail and PARKED is misclassified as LIKELY-FROZEN -> agent killed while correctly waiting. The fast path `classify_log_line` (1613-1630) uses `session.id=` regex only; mismatch between the two attribution paths produces unattributed PARKED alerts (`[FAST] PARKED-RETRYING detected (unattributed session …)`) that never park the actual agent. Add a fallback that attributes by worktree slug substring match when `session.id` unresolvable, and fail-open to PARKED bias (do not kill when rate-limit words present).\n\n**F-M7 — `OBSERVER_DIS_VALIDATOR` vs `OBSERVER_MODELS_CMD` escaping: whitespace-split command loses quoting and cannot carry args with spaces or `|`**. `run([DIS_VALIDATOR, REPO_ROOT, doc])` (1528-1531) execs validator as `[\"/path/with spaces/validator\", …]` via list, so spaces would survive if the exec path were split correctly, but `load_catalog` does `MODELS_CMD_TMPL.replace(...).split()` (2188) which discards shell quoting — `opencode models \"opencode-go\"` becomes `['opencode','models','\"opencode-go\"']` (quotes become literal). Today the templates are simple (`opencode models {provider}` / `bash /…/fake-models.sh {provider}`) so tests pass, but the contract `OBSERVER_MODELS_CMD` “overridable for tests” invites a quoted override that will silently return empty catalog → `model_valid` returns None (indecisive) → violations suppressed. Document that the template is whitespace-tokenized not shell-parsed, or use `shlex.split`.\n\n**F-M8 — Harness covers the happy path but never fault-injects the `RED` verification or `rclone` positive sync branches.** `run-tests.sh` T15 asserts GREEN/pending/prune GREEN, never flips a byte to force sha256 mismatch, never populates a fake `rclone` remote. The python `verify_export_readback` RED path (1955-1963) and `rclone_sync_and_verify` positive path (1934-1965) are thus inspected-only, matching the builder’s own `WHAT-NOT-TESTED` (`RED verification branch not fault-injected; real rclone remote sync (no remote wired)`). Not a code bug but a claim-risk: the green-gated safety property that gates deletion/pruning has no executable proof on this branch.\n\n### MINOR\n\n**F-N1 — `scan_doctrine_files` depth 4 + cap 800 can miss nested doctrine files; missing dependents silently skip validation.** `walk` (1405) depth>4 returns; repos deeper than 4 levels lose doctrine snapshots. Acceptable for current layout but undocumented.\n\n**F-N2 — `working_issue` regex `\\*\\*Issue\\*\\*:\\s*#(\\d+)` fails on `KICKOFF.md` that writes `Issue: 460` without bold markers** (alternative template in issue #449). `act_*` then posts to `FLAG_ISSUE` (429) instead of the agent’s working issue, diluting per-issue evidence.\n\n**F-N3 — `hot_copy_store` constructs `.backup` argument as `\".backup \" + dest` (1792) — a single sqlite3 dot-command string.** Works with the `sqlite3` CLI but couples to sqlite3’s argument parsing; using `\".backup\", dest` two-args variant would be more robust across sqlite builds.\n\n**F-N4 — `read_new_log_lines` silently baselines on first sight and on inode rotation, losing failures that occur in the baseline window.** By design (never classify history), but means a rate-limit that occurs during an Observer restart is never parked; the agent will be judged FROZEN one cycle later. Documented as cheap-staleness trigger trade-off.\n\n**F-N5 — Test harness `T5/T13` log fixtures embed `retry-after: 2026-08-24 09:30` (no timezone) — parsed as UTC** (591-597) then compared to `time.time()` (1237). If the test machine’s log timestamps are in local time, the parsed epoch drifts by the TZ offset, causing spurious expiry in CI. Use `Z` suffix or explicit offset.\n\n**F-N6 — `verify_log_line` + `sync-pending.log` + `prune-report.txt` use `now_iso()` per row, so events within one backup pass have slightly different stamps, breaking “one pass” correlation.** Cosmetic; prefer one `pass_ts` per wave.\n\n---\n\n## 3 — Error-handling sweep (every external binary surface)\n\n| Surface | Failure mode | Handled? |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crosslink issue comment` | rc≠0 / binary missing / timeout | logged `comment posted:false` + rc/err (503-505), NOT surfaced to operator (F-M1) |\n| `crosslink kickoff cleanup / stop` | rc≠0 / missing | logged, bool returned, orphan flagged next cycle, no re-alert (F-C1/F-M1) |\n| `crosslink issue show` / `locks check` | rc≠0 / parse misses | `working_issue` returns None→FLAG, `admission_checks` counts as fail (correct) |\n| `git rev-parse / rev-list / merge-base / diff / cat-file / log` | rc≠0 / timeout / missing | per-call rc checks; `branch None`→`deliverable_present False` correct; `ahead_of_main None` silently skips push suggest |\n| `sqlite3 .backup` | missing binary / disk full / integrity fail | rc/message logged (1792-1806), `pass_ok False`, no operator comment (F-M1) |\n| `sqlite3 PRAGMA integrity_check` | row≠\"ok\" | treated as copy failure (1801-1802) correct |\n| `tmux list-panes / capture-pane` | missing / no server / gone | returns gone/None placeholder (618-644) correct, but conflates missing tmux with gone |\n| `rclone listremotes / copy / cat` | missing / no remotes / network | `rclone_remote_ready False`→pending path (1920-1931) correct; copy/cat failures → `backup-sync-failed` event only (2090-2092) |\n| `opencode models {provider}` | timeout / parse empty | `load_catalog` stores empty lists, returns None→`model_valid` indecisive (non-blocking) correct but silent (F-M7) |\n| `hashlib.sha256 / gzip / os.stat` | OSError | caught per call (772, 1706, 1639) with event |\n\nMissing: `crosslink sync` never invoked by Observer (intentional — mutations via CLI only); sync deferral means posted evidence/comments may remain hub-cache-local until operator syncs.\n\n---\n\n## 4 — Uncaught exceptions / `set -u` / grep misses / exit codes\n\n- `set -u` (NOT `set -e`) correctly avoids aborting on signal-trap, but bare `${VAR}` without `:-` appears in `discover_repo_root` (279-295) and `STORES` loop (382-386) where an unset `OB_STORES` would trip nounset; mitigated because defaults are set at top (185-242). However `OB_REPO_ROOT` delay-assign (294) reads `OBSERVER_REPO_ROOT` which may be unset — guarded via `${OBSERVER_REPO_ROOT:-…}` so safe.\n- Embedded Python `run()` catches `FileNotFoundError`->127 and `TimeoutExpired`->124, but the outer bash `liveness_rc=$?` branch (2455) only treats non-zero rc or empty out as error; a `TimeoutExpired` from `agent-liveness.py` yields rc 124 which is correctly counted as `consecutive_errors`. A `FileNotFoundError` for `python3` itself would propagate as rc 127 at the bash level if `python3` missing? Actually `out=\"$(python3 …)\"` captures stderr, rc is the shell’s last command rc — missing `python3` returns 127, correctly counted.\n- `grep` misses: `grep -a -E` returns 1 when no match (not error). Code correctly gates on `rc==0 and out` (528-534, 546-549). `rc==2` syntax errors are also treated as “not found” and swallowed — low risk (patterns are literals + `re.escape(agent)`).\n- `python -c 'json.dumps(json.load(sys.stdin)…)'` (2469-2471) : on malformed liveness JSON, `compact` becomes empty, triggers `json-parse-failed` (2472) but still `consecutive_errors` was reset to 0 at 2466 before the branch. Follow-on Python `python -c \"$CYCLE_PROG\"` (2475) may still be invoked with empty `compact` (it would hit `data.get(\"agents\",[])` with invalid JSON stream → `cycle-input-invalid` (2321-2325)). The consecutive-error cap should include json-parse failures.\n\n---\n\n## 5 — Races, idempotency, tamper, growth, claims\n\n- **Races:** Single-writer assumption holds (one Observer per `OBSERVER_STATE_DIR`). Concurrent Observers on same dir would interleave `manager-state.json.tmp` replaces; no flock. Document single-instance requirement. `read_new_log_lines` is race-free against log rotation via inode+offset (1638-1644) but truncated-in-place reset (`offset > size → 0`) races with a writer that truncates then appends quickly: first cycle after truncate may read a partial line that lacks its trailing `\\n` and is never re-read (FAST_READ_CAP cap path’s `rfind`). Low probability.\n- **Idempotency:** Per-agent dedup is prefix-correct (`handled` set) but breaker coupling breaks idempotency on partial failure (F-C1). Backup is idempotent only when GREEN; RED causes re-export loop (F-M4). Wave-anomaly dedup is per-episode correctly.\n- **Tamper:** see F-C3.\n- **Growth:** see F-M5.\n- **Claims vs code:** “all mutations via crosslink CLI” holds (grep: only `crosslink kickoff …`, `crosslink issue comment`, `crosslink locks check` are mutating). “everything evidence-hashed” overstates — only evidence bundles are hashed; manager-state, watermarks, and `verification.log` entries are not chained. “surface-independent across OpenCode v1/v2” holds for the polling/byte-offset core but attribution (F-M6) is still schema-coupled.\n\n---\n\n## 6 — Harness assessment (`tests/run-tests.sh`)\n\nPassing 98/98 is load-bearing for this verdict. Coverage is strong on transitions (T1-T7 per-verdict, T4 real tmux, T5 park expiry, T12 evidence sections, T13 dedup, T14 commit-age grace, T15 dual-store Green/incr/cap, T16 live issue-exists/claimed, T17 anomaly dedup/re-arm). Gaps noted: no fault injection for RED/sha256-mismatch, no positive `rclone cat` path, no multi-day archive traversal, no concurrent Observer. The `OBSERVER_BACKUP_ENABLED=0` default guard (74,390) correctly avoids churning real stores on fresh dirs — a bug the builder discovered and fixed. Minor: `check_absent` (35) and `check` greps are unanchored substrings, so a stray log line containing the pattern elsewhere could yield false PASS.\n\n---\n\nWHY: The six-verdict supervisor contracts (kill-with-evidence on confirmed-frozen per #443 rev3, park-instead-of-kill on rate-limited, dual-store verified incremental export with GREEN-gated pruning, pre-dispatch admission checks without new plugins, wave-anomaly alerts, and evidence-at-every-terminal-transition) are all mechanically present and pairwise wired to the liveness walk + byte-offset fast path. The remaining risks are failure-propagation and durability (silent breaker gating, state-file loss, unbounded logs, /tmp trust).\n\nWHAT: Verdict evidence is the code itself at `main` HEAD (`scripts/observer/observer.sh` 2489 lines, `tests/run-tests.sh` 528 lines, `agent-liveness.py v2` six-class matrix unchanged) plus the three background specs read in full (lifecycle-manager-design.md SC1-SC5, #460 dispatch plan comment 2026-08-24 10:54 (R1-R4, F1-F6), `.crosslink/knowledge/data-retention.md` 12 lines). Harness is 98/98 green on the committed tree.\n\nHOW-CERTAIN: Evidence-based for every line-cited finding (file:line references checked against `main` HEAD); consequence severity (CRITICAL/MAJOR/MINOR) is reasoned inference from failure-mode analysis, not live-fault injection (RED/rclone positive paths, multi-hour soak, concurrent writers, permission tamper not executed). Certainty: high that listed code paths exist; medium that the assessed blast radius matches production waves.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: RED verification branch fault-injection (sha256/row-count mismatch) and its watermark-hold/prune-gate interaction; real `rclone` remote sync positive path and `rclone cat` hash agreement with remote; non-dry-run mutating paths end-to-end (real `crosslink kickoff cleanup/stop` + hub-visible comments); long-duration loop behavior with `OBSERVER_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MINS=1440` gating and multi-day archive rotation; concurrent Observers on the same state dir; opencode.log schema drift across OpenCode v1/v2; actual `opencode.db` (2.6GB) + `opencode-fork-pp3g.db` (2.9GB) hot-backup load/IO timing on this host.","created_at":"2026-08-25T02:54:34.967573519Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:yY9s5rFqOO/BpO2Jzd2UYG25/EFrjSwlsbHKiRNiy0E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5xuy9LOVXEIsmuwJJoKXWuaVTmLpEo742XDTNRo5+kAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAriE3JliSgyEBSh1fvCKgSs8pbZbfKyinkY4DdFRz+ykiLj58GXzsXtwV788uVs0foHEhaumrc1VyBzfbLEm6AQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:yY9s5rFqOO/BpO2Jzd2UYG25/EFrjSwlsbHKiRNiy0E","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5xuy9LOVXEIsmuwJJoKXWuaVTmLpEo742XDTNRo5+kAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPqcVE/lBvGp2CgtSI6k9B7uFx3DPIYikJ2Ijb8pDCy0ldJjWw4H7PuQRXAuV666ryWpy9CQoMsmls6FKloS/A8="}
